nt a denial.\\n\\nThe available GPS data directly contradicts the deviation flags applied to these legs. The breadcrumbs confirm that pickups and routes align with what would be expected for legitimate service at this address. Based on the documented GPS evidence and applicable guidelines, both trips are valid and we request that they be approved accordingly.\",\"aiBaselineSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1862897820 - GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence (2 rides)\",\"aiBaselineDescriptionHtml\":\"We are disputing the GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence flags on invoice 1862897820, covering Conf #15028977 and Conf #15028974, both serviced on 2026-04-27, and requesting that these trips be reconsidered for approval.\\n\\nFor both rides, GPS breadcrumb data is available and was reviewed. On Conf #15028977 (Car 3079), the breadcrumb trail reasonably supports pickup at or near the member's residence, indicating no true deviation occurred. On Conf #15028974 (Car 1602), the GPS route supports valid trip completion from pickup to drop-off, with no evidence of a routing irregularity that would warrant a denial.\\n\\nThe available GPS data directly contradicts the deviation flags applied to these legs. The breadcrumbs confirm that pickups and routes align with what would be expected for legitimate service at this address. Based on the documented GPS evidence and applicable guidelines, both trips are valid and we request that they be approved accordingly.\",\"draftAttribution\":null,\"draftEditedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:07:39.980Z\",\"draftEditedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"draftReviewedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:07:39.980Z\",\"draftReviewedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"specialCircumstances\":null,\"understandingReadback\":null,\"understandingReadbackForText\":null,\"understandingReadbackAt\":null,\"understandingReadbackBy\":null,\"previewGeneratedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:07:39.980Z\",\"previewGeneratedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"reattestRequired\":true,\"reattestCompletedAt\":\"2026-05-14T14:0