9\",\"rideCount\":2,\"serviceDate\":\"2026-04-27\",\"totalAmount\":\"72.99\",\"groupContext\":null,\"draftSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1869698530 - Incomplete GPS (2 rides)\",\"draftDescriptionHtml\":\"Reconsideration Request – Incomplete GPS – Invoice #1869698530\\n\\nWe are disputing the Incomplete GPS flag on invoice #1869698530 and requesting reconsideration for Conf #15064750 and Conf #15064749, both serviced on 04/27/2026.\\n\\nBoth trips have GPS breadcrumb data on file, and that data is sufficient to reasonably support trip completion for each leg. The Incomplete GPS edit does not reflect a true deviation here -- the routes are traceable and the documentation supports that both transports were carried out as authorized.\\n\\nThe attached GPS records for vehicles 336 and 2637 confirm coverage along the trip routes for each confirmation. Based on this documentation, both claims are valid and we request that they be approved accordingly.\",\"aiBaselineSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1869698530 - Incomplete GPS (2 rides)\",\"aiBaselineDescriptionHtml\":\"**Reconsideration Request – Incomplete GPS – Invoice #1869698530**\\n\\nWe are disputing the Incomplete GPS flag on invoice #1869698530 and requesting reconsideration for Conf #15064750 and Conf #15064749, both serviced on 04/27/2026.\\n\\nBoth trips have GPS breadcrumb data on file, and that data is sufficient to reasonably support trip completion for each leg. The Incomplete GPS edit does not reflect a true deviation here -- the routes are traceable and the documentation supports that both transports were carried out as authorized.\\n\\nThe attached GPS records for vehicles 336 and 2637 confirm coverage along the trip routes for each confirmation. Based on this documentation, both claims are valid and we request that they be approved accordingly.\",\"draftAttribution\":null,\"draftEditedAt\":\"2026-05-09T18:33:17.468Z\",\"draftEditedBy\":\"KATIA.H@AGAPENY.COM\",\"draftReviewedAt\":\"2026-05-09T18:33:19.519Z\"