p\":{\"id\":1071,\"invoiceNumber\":\"1868985360\",\"clientNumber\":\"HN30192V\",\"errorDetails\":\"GPS pickup too far from residence; Travel time is too short for distance traveled; Leg is in GPS Deviation Status.\",\"errorTypeId\":\"6\",\"errorTypeName\":\"GPS Deviation Status\",\"status\":\"Resolved\",\"outcome\":\"Approved\",\"phase\":\"closed\",\"phaseEnteredAt\":\"2026-05-14T14:31:58.333Z\",\"approvedAmount\":\"243.03\",\"rideCount\":2,\"serviceDate\":\"2026-04-27\",\"totalAmount\":\"243.03\",\"groupContext\":null,\"draftSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1868985360 - GPS Deviation Status (2 rides)\",\"draftDescriptionHtml\":\"We are disputing the GPS Deviation Status flags on invoice 1868985360, covering two trips for client HN30192V: Conf #15055719 (Car 381) and Conf #15055720 (Car 405), and requesting that both claims be reconsidered for approval.\\n\\nFor Conf #15055719, the recorded travel time was reviewed against the trip distance and reasonably supports the route as completed. The timing data is available and accounts for the flagged discrepancy, confirming this is not a true deviation. For Conf #15055720, available GPS breadcrumb data shows a route that logically and consistently supports a valid trip from pickup to drop-off, which directly contradicts the basis for the deviation flag.\\n\\nThe supporting GPS and timing data for both trips demonstrate that transportation was completed as authorized. There is no substantive basis for the deviation status on either leg, and we request that both claims be approved in accordance with the documentation on file.\",\"aiBaselineSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1868985360 - GPS Deviation Status (2 rides)\",\"aiBaselineDescriptionHtml\":\"We are disputing the GPS Deviation Status flags on invoice 1868985360, covering two trips for client HN30192V: Conf #15055719 (Car 381) and Conf #15055720 (Car 405), and requesting that both claims be reconsidered for approval.\\n\\nFor Conf #15055719, the recorded travel time was reviewed against the trip distance and reasonably supports the route as completed. The timing data is available and accounts for the flagged discrepancy, confirming this is not a true deviation. For Conf #15055720, available GPS breadcrumb data shows a route that logically and consistently supports a valid trip from pickup to drop-off, which directly contradicts the basis for the deviation flag.\\n\\nThe supporting GPS and timing data for both trips demonstrate that transportation was completed as authorized. There is no substantive basis for the deviation status on either leg, and we request that both claims be approved in accordance with the documentation on file.\",\"draftAttribution\":null,\"draftEditedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:08:22.581Z\",\"draftEditedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"draftReviewedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:08:22.581Z\",\"draftReviewedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"specialCircumstances\":null,\"understandingReadback\":null,\"understandingReadbackForText\":null,\"understandingReadbackAt\":null,\"understandingReadbackBy\":null,\"previewGeneratedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:08:22.581Z\",\"previewGeneratedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"reattestRequired\":true,\"reattestCompletedAt\":\"2026-05-14T14:31:58.301Z\",\"reattestCompletedBy\":\"someidy.s@agapeny.com\",\"reattestNote\":null,\"holdReason\":null,\"holdPendingFrom\":null,\"holdPlacedAt\":null,\"triageNotes\":null,\"triagedAt\":null,\"closureReason\":\"reattested\",\"closureCategory\":null,\"closureCategoryOther\":null,\"closureRootCause\":null,\"closureRootCauseOther\":null,\"closureNarrative\":null,\"closureAccountabilityTags\":null,\"closureAccountabilityOther\":null,\"closureDrivers\":null,\"closureDispatchers\":null,\"closureCommunicatedTo\":null,\"closureResponsibility\":null,\"closureReviewState\":null,\"closureAddressedAt\":null,\"closureAddressedBy\":null,\"closureAddressedByEmail\":null,\"closureReviewNotes\":null,\"disputeEmailSent\":true,\"disputeEmailSentAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:32:50.040Z\",\"generatedEmailSub