tedAt\":\"2026-05-14T14:32:03.415Z\"},\"attestationOutcome\":\"attested\",\"outcomeAt\":\"2026-05-14T14:32:03.415Z\",\"outcomeBy\":\"someidy.s@agapeny.com\",\"outcomeNote\":null}]},{\"group\":{\"id\":1072,\"invoiceNumber\":\"1844199410\",\"clientNumber\":\"VM75096H\",\"errorDetails\":\"GPS pickup too far from medical facility; Leg is in GPS Deviation Status.\",\"errorTypeId\":\"4\",\"errorTypeName\":\"GPS Pickup Too Far from Medical Facility\",\"status\":\"Resolved\",\"outcome\":\"Approved\",\"phase\":\"closed\",\"phaseEnteredAt\":\"2026-05-14T14:29:56.986Z\",\"approvedAmount\":\"60.10\",\"rideCount\":2,\"serviceDate\":\"2026-04-27\",\"totalAmount\":\"60.10\",\"groupContext\":null,\"draftSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1844199410 - GPS Pickup Too Far from Medical Facility (2 rides)\",\"draftDescriptionHtml\":\"We are disputing the GPS Pickup Too Far from Medical Facility flags on invoice 1844199410, covering Conf #15029348 and Conf #15029346, and requesting that both claims be reconsidered for approval.\\n\\nFor Conf #15029348 (Car 5097), GPS breadcrumb data is available and reasonably supports pickup at or near the medical facility. The flagged deviation does not reflect what the route data actually shows. For Conf #15029346 (Car 492), breadcrumb data is likewise available and confirms a valid route from pickup to drop-off, consistent with a completed trip. In both cases, the GPS Deviation Status appears to be a system-generated flag that is contradicted by the underlying location data.\\n\\nThe attached GPS breadcrumb records for each leg demonstrate that pickups occurred within an acceptable range of the medical facility and that both trips were completed as authorized. Based on this documentation, neither flag represents a true deviation, and we request that both confirmations on this invoice be approved accordingly.\",\"aiBaselineSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1844199410 - GPS Pickup Too Far from Medical Facility (2 rides)\",\"aiBaselineDescriptionHtml\":\"We are disputing the GPS Pickup Too Far from Medical Facility flags on invoice 1844199410, covering Conf #15029348 and Conf #15029346, and requesting that both claims be reconsidered for approval.\\n\\nFor Conf #15029348 (Car 5097), GPS breadcrumb data is available and reasonably supports pickup at or near the medical facility. The flagged deviation does not reflect what the route data actually shows. For Conf #15029346 (Car 492), breadcrumb data is likewise available and confirms a valid route from pickup to drop-off, consistent with a completed trip. In both cases, the GPS Deviation Status appears to be a system-generated flag that is contradicted by the underlying location data.\\n\\nThe attached GPS breadcrumb records for each leg demonstrate that pickups occurred within an acceptable range of the medical facility and that both trips were completed as authorized. Based on this documentation, neither flag represents a true deviation, and we request that both confirmations on this invoice be approved accordingly.\",\"draftAttribution\":null,\"draftEditedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:08:15.448Z\",\"draftEditedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"draftReviewedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:08:15.448Z\",\"draftReviewedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"specialCircumstances\":null,\"understandingReadback\":null,\"understandingReadbackForText\":null,\"understandingReadbackAt\":null,\"understandingReadbackBy\":null,\"previewGeneratedAt\":\"2026-05-09T23:08:15.448Z\",\"previewGeneratedBy\":\"emil.j@agapeny.com\",\"reattestRequired\":true,\"reattestCompletedAt\":\"2026-05-14T14:29:56.953Z\",\"reattestCompletedBy\":\"someidy.s@agapeny.com\",\"reattestNote\":null,\"holdReason\":null,\"holdPendingFrom\":null,\"holdPlacedAt\":null,\"triageNotes\":null,\"triagedAt\":null,\"closureReason\":\"reattested\",\"closureCategory\":null,\"closureCategoryOther\":null,\"closureRootCause\":null,\"closureRootCauseOther\":null,\"closureNarrative\":null,\"closureAccountabilityTags\":null,\"closureAccountabilityOther\":null,\"c