pdatedAt\":\"2026-05-10T01:55:01.338Z\"},\"attestationOutcome\":\"attested\",\"outcomeAt\":\"2026-05-07T22:24:28.455Z\",\"outcomeBy\":\"Grace@agapeny.com\",\"outcomeNote\":null}]},{\"group\":{\"id\":303,\"invoiceNumber\":\"1857451670\",\"clientNumber\":\"UW74354J\",\"errorDetails\":\"GPS pickup too far from residence; Leg is in GPS Deviation Status.\",\"errorTypeId\":\"3\",\"errorTypeName\":\"GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence\",\"status\":\"Resolved\",\"outcome\":\"Approved\",\"phase\":\"closed\",\"phaseEnteredAt\":\"2026-05-07T00:50:57.113Z\",\"approvedAmount\":\"116.14\",\"rideCount\":2,\"serviceDate\":\"2026-04-06\",\"totalAmount\":\"116.14\",\"groupContext\":null,\"draftSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1857451670 - GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence (2 rides)\",\"draftDescriptionHtml\":\"**Subject: Dispute – GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence – Invoice #1857451670**\\n\\nWe are disputing the GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence flags on Invoice #1857451670, which affected two trips: Conf #14918026 and Conf #14918028, both serviced on 04/06/2026. We are requesting that both legs be reconsidered and approved for submission.\\n\\nFor Conf #14918026 (Car 3079), GPS breadcrumb data is available and reasonably supports that pickup occurred at or near the member's residence. The deviation flag does not reflect the actual route data. Similarly, for Conf #14918028 (Car 1106), the full GPS route supports a valid trip between the pickup and dropoff locations, confirming that the trip was completed as intended.\\n\\nThe attached GPS breadcrumb data for both trips directly contradicts the deviation status assigned to each leg. The data shows compliant pickup placement and logical routing throughout, leaving no factual basis for the GPS deviation flags. These are valid, completed trips and we request that both claims be approved in accordance with the supporting documentation.\",\"aiBaselineSubject\":\"Dispute - Invoice #1857451670 - GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence (2 rides)\",\"aiBaselineDescriptionHtml\":\"**Subject: Dispute – GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence – Invoice #1857451670**\\n\\nWe are disputing the GPS Pickup Too Far from Residence flags on Invoice #1857451670, which affected two trips: Conf #14918026 and Conf #14918028, both serviced on 04/06/2026. We are requesting that both legs be reconsidered and approved for submission.\\n\\nFor Conf #14918026 (Car 3079), GPS breadcrumb data is available and reasonably supports that pickup occurred at or near the member's residence. The deviation flag does not reflect the actual route data. Similarly, for Conf #14918028 (Car 1106), the full GPS route supports a valid trip between the pickup and dropoff locations, confirming that the trip was completed as intended.\\n\\nThe attached GPS breadcrumb data for both trips directly contradicts the deviation status assigned to each leg. The data shows compliant pickup placement and logical routing throughout, leaving no factual basis for the GPS deviation flags. These are valid, completed trips and we request that both claims be approved in accordance with the supporting documentation.\",\"draftAttribution\":null,\"draftEditedAt\":\"2026-05-06T14:14:44.370Z\",\"draftEditedBy\":\"someidy.s@agapeny.com\",\"draftReviewedAt\":\"2026-05-06T14:14:49.450Z\",\"draftReviewedBy\":\"someidy.s@agapeny.com\",\"specialCircumstances\":null,\"understandingReadback\":null,\"understandingReadbackForText\":null,\"understandingReadbackAt\":null,\"understandingReadbackBy\":null,\"previewGeneratedAt\":\"2026-05-06T14:14:44.370Z\",\"previewGeneratedBy\":\"someidy.s@agapeny.com\",\"reattestRequired\":true,\"reattestCompletedAt\":\"2026-05-07T22:24:18.026Z\",\"reattestCompletedBy\":null,\"reattestNote\":null,\"holdReason\":null,\"holdPendingFrom\":null,\"holdPlacedAt\":null,\"triageNotes\":null,\"triagedAt\":null,\"closureReason\":\"reattested\",\"closureCategory\":null,\"closureCategoryOther\":null,\"closureRootCause\":null,\"closureRootCauseOther\":null,\"closureNarrati